 36S  c  1971Ol02: E=3.12, 3.28, and 3.40 MeV triton beams with an intensity of 
 36S 2c  |?40 nA were produced from the 3.5-MV Van de Graaff accelerator at     
 36S 3c  Brookhaven National Laboratory. Targets were 200-600-|mg/cm{+2}        
 36S 4c  Sb{-2}S{-3} enriched to 85.61% in {+34}S on 70-|mg/cm{+2} Mo,          
 36S 5c  2-mg/cm{+2} Au, or 1.7-mg/cm{+2} Ni backings. Protons from             
 36S 6c  {+34}S(t,p|g){+36}S were detected using a 900-|mm-thick annular Si     
 36S 7c  detector covering 165|'-170|', and at 135|' using a Si detector with   
 36S 8c  FWHM=30 keV. |g rays were detected using a 5|*6-in. NaI(Tl) detector at
 36S 9c  0|'-90|' and a 40-cm{+3} Ge(Li) detector at 0|'-140|' with FWHM=1.9    
 36S Ac  keV. Internal pairs were detected using an intermediate-image pair     
 36S Bc  spectrometer. 511-keV annihilation |g rays were detected using a       
 36S Cc  3|*2-in. plastic scintillator in delayed coincidence. Measured E{-p},  
 36S Dc  I{-p}, E|g, I|g, p|g-coin, and |g|g-coin. Deduced levels, J, |p, and   
 36S Ec  |g-ray multipolarities.                                                
 36S  c  1971Ju02: E=3.1 MeV triton beam with an intensity of |?80 nA was       
 36S 2c  provided from the 3-MV Van de Graaff accelerator at the Nuclear        
 36S 3c  Research Center in Strasbourg, France. The target was a 500-|mg/cm{+2} 
 36S 4c  Sb{-2}S{-3} layer enriched to 85% in {+34}S on a 30-|mm Mo backing.    
 36S 5c  Protons from {+34}S(t,p|g){+36}S were detected at 180|' using an       
 36S 6c  annular 200-mm{+2}, 1-mm-thick Si detector placed 8 mm behind the      
 36S 7c  target and covered by a 30-|mm Al absorber. |g rays were detected using
 36S 8c  a Compton polarimeter consisting of a central 3.8-cm-dia, 7.6-cm       
 36S 9c  NaI(Tl) detector at 90|' and two 7.6|*7.6-cm NaI(Tl) detectors parallel
 36S Ac  and perpendicular to the reaction plane. Measured p-|g-Compton triple  
 36S Bc  coincidences and linear polarizations. Deduced levels, J, |p, and      
 36S Cc  |g-ray multipolarities.                                                
